WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.450
- [Woman] I wish I had
Naruto's Shadow Clone Jutsu

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.060
cause it's definitely gonna take more

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.570
than one of me to get this stuff done.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:06.478
I mean come--

00:00:06.478 --> 00:00:07.760
(bangs)

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:08.593
- [Clone] Hello.

00:00:08.593 --> 00:00:09.713
- [Woman] Whoa.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.630
Hello, everyone, it is me, Élise.

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:15.036
And today,

00:00:15.036 --> 00:00:17.030
(fist banging on counter)

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:19.830
I am making every single dish from Naruto.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.630
Naruto is a very popular anime

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.540
so if you don't know what it is

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.500
I don't know what to tell you.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.600
Naruto's favorite food is what?

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.660
Ramen? Yes.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.270
That's obviously what most people think

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.940
about what there are so many
other foods that appear.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.050
So I am going to take it upon myself

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.890
to show you every single
thing from this anime.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:38.240
It's gonna to be a great time.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.080
So in Naruto, in the anime
and in the filler episodes,

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:44.008
you can see them eating
something called mitarashi dango

00:00:44.008 --> 00:00:44.841
and Hanami Dango.

00:00:44.841 --> 00:00:47.400
For this one today, I'm gonna
to make the mitarashi one.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.190
So, let's do it!

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:51.330
Okay, so in my bowl here,

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.160
I have the Mochiko sweet rice flour.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.360
- [Élise Voiceover] Gradually add water.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.100
- We kind of want to get
like a cookie dough texture.

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.320
So I got the texture.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.970
Now, I have to roll it
into one-inch balls.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:04.600
Then they're going to boil in some water.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.330
- [Élise Voiceover] When they're
done cool in a nice bath,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.720
and for the glaze you'll need

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.860
sugar, soy sauce, mirin and cornstarch.

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.070
Stir until thickened.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.150
- The mochi is done.

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:16.180
Usually there's about three
to four mochi on one skewer.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.410
This is kind of long.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.699
I'm going to put three on this.

00:01:19.699 --> 00:01:21.090
(excited yell)

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.220
All I have to do is pour the sauce on it.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:25.410
Oh, yeah!

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.780
Me and my mitarashi dango.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:28.630
I'm going to try it.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.190
It's dripping all over my hand.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.023
Oh!

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:33.720
I enjoy this a lot.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:34.553
I'm going to eat this.

00:01:34.553 --> 00:01:35.930
I'll just have to make another one.

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.070
All right, there's lots of
other stuff that I gotta make.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.070
Let's go!

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:41.280
I'm going to be making the fried rice

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.380
that Itachi made for Sasuke

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.010
when he made a big meal
when they were a kid.

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:46.440
And I'm excited to make this one

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.060
because I get to use my wok.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.690
I'm going to start with some butter.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:52.800
I got two eggs.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.223
Egg crack, one-handed.

00:01:56.054 --> 00:01:57.020
Oh!

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.930
Gonna stir fry that up.

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:01.020
Onions in.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.280
All right, this has been
saucin' for a little bit.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:04.880
I got some precooked rice.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.033
I gotta throw that in there.

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.190
(clanging)

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:10.180
I forgot the garlic! I can
still throw it in, right?

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.510
I got some soy sauce, sesame
oil, and a little bit of mirin.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.617
Get a little sweetness in the fried rice.

00:02:15.617 --> 00:02:16.450
Yeah!

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.440
Just a little bit of mirin, sesame oil.

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.920
I forgot to cut the green onions.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.483
So that's what I'm doing now.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.780
Oh, yeah!

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:28.080
That's what they call fried rice.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.313
I should taste this.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.273
It's good.

00:02:33.273 --> 00:02:35.810
Okay, so the fried rice is complete

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:39.130
and I am just pouring it into this bowl

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.790
because the way Itachi has it set up

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:44.720
is in like a big, large mound.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.070
Pat that in there.

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.100
All right, we're gonna to pour it out.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.520
Let's see what happens.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:49.353
Here we go.

00:02:49.353 --> 00:02:51.017
And,

00:02:51.017 --> 00:02:52.290
voila!

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:55.740
Our fried rice is here and ready to enjoy.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:56.573
Not yet.

00:02:56.573 --> 00:02:57.900
I got a lot of other stuff to make.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:58.840
Let's go!

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.600
Briefly interrupting to catch
you guys up on the ramen.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.940
I know that's why you
clicked on this video.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:03.820
That's what you wanna see.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.100
And yes, I am making traditional ramen.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.280
And yes, it does take 12 hours.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.500
We're gonna go back to the past.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.740
We're gonna talk to past Élise

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:12.830
and she's gonna show us how
she made the ramen broth.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:13.850
And then we're gonna keep it going.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:15.927
Past Élise!

00:03:15.927 --> 00:03:17.500
(heavy sigh)

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.710
It's me, past Élise.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:21.310
You know, I'm up at 6:00 AM in the morning

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.480
to make some broth.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.450
Let's get started.

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.110
Okay. So since I'm making a
traditional tonkotsu broth

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:27.330
I have to use pork.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:30.560
I got some pigs' feet, and I also got

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.360
some pig neck bones.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.580
- [Élise Voiceover]
Rinse the pork real quick

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.010
and then add fresh water to boil.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.430
- We're gonna take this to the stove.

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:39.480
Let this boil for like 10 minutes or so.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.550
To like grow stuff from the pig's feet,

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.510
and the neck bones are
gonna like come to the top.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:44.470
We're gonna skim it off.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.510
And then we will be
ready to make the broth.

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.900
So while the meat is boiling at--

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:50.140
Get out.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:54.600
I got the onions, scallions, green onion,

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:59.600
some knobs of ginger,
garlic, a leek and a--

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.270
What is this?

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:02.960
Bok choy. Bok choy!

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:06.520
These go in the soup
and help give it flavor.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:10.960
I'm now putting in nice and
fresh water for the broth.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.330
Let me stop screaming.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:16.850
I can also add in all my
vegetables. The broth is clear.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:19.270
The bones are in. All
the vegetables are there.

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:22.902
This is now going to cook for 12 hours.

00:04:22.902 --> 00:04:24.300
(yelling)

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.130
Now, back to present Élise.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.590
Our ramen is going strong.

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:30.830
Come look at it.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.900
Mr. Ramen is doing what it's gotta do.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:37.221
All right, so now I'm
going to make the onigiri.

00:04:37.221 --> 00:04:39.230
This should be relatively easy.

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.710
So I wet my hands.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.990
Now I'm just going to
mold the rice together.

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:46.270
You gotta make like a triangle type shape.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.360
The shaping it isn't too difficult.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.390
♪At the carwash ♪

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.940
All right, that's our bottom half.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:56.650
Traditionally, it's stuffed
with a pickled plum.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.650
The umeboshi, so I'm gonna
put that right in the center.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.270
The one that Hinata makes

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.320
doesn't look like it's a stuffed one.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.210
It looks like she put
all the like fillings

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.444
and stuff on the top, but either way,

00:05:07.444 --> 00:05:08.930
that's what we're doing.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:11.330
And I'm gonna cover it
with this rice here,

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:13.786
forcefully mold, everything together.

00:05:13.786 --> 00:05:15.400
(yelling)

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.310
We're going to decorate
it to look like Naruto.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.910
- [Élise Voiceover] I
used carrots for his ears

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:22.350
and seaweed for his eyes,
whiskers and headband.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.600
- We kinda got a smile going on.

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:26.100
Damn it, I broke it!

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:30.683
On his headband, she
used a piece of Naruto,

00:05:31.618 --> 00:05:32.770
(laughing) namesake.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.610
This is a fish cake, which
is also called Narutomaki.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:38.840
And she used this to be like
the leaf village head symbol.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:42.870
Damn it, I just realized his
hair. I can use the radish.

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.600
Okay. Okay!

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.580
We're getting somewhe--

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.600
Honestly, I will say hers is
a lot better than mine. It is.

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:53.110
It doesn't look anything like him.

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:54.210
It's the thought that counts.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:59.210
So now I'm going to make the
bento box from the bell scene.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:00.860
That's what I'm making. Okay. Let's do it!

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.580
So the bento box is really easy.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:05.140
I have this little square box here.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.540
So we got some rice here.

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:08.880
Pack that to the side.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.950
I wish my bento box had a
divider like theirs does.

00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.580
This is just a rectangle.

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:18.420
And in the center of the
rice, they have pickled plums.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:21.800
I'm going to put one of
those right in the center.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:24.010
They got some vegetables
over there on the side.

00:06:24.010 --> 00:06:27.430
So I sautéed some oranges.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:28.530
This is not an orange.

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:31.270
I sautéed some carrots
and onions together,

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:34.100
and that'll be our little
vegetable mixture on the side.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.490
I also have some pickled radish here.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:38.740
I'm going to put some of
that in there as well.

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:40.610
Why? Just because.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:44.370
And last, but of course not
least we have a boiled egg.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.000
Nice and beautiful and boiled.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.900
We're going to split this
in half. Right there.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:53.860
Beautiful. The bento box is now complete.

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:56.190
I guess I can try.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:58.793
I've never had a pickled radish before.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.740
I have had a pickled radish before.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:06.313
Me and my boiled egg say, cheers.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:11.500
I'm gonna et this down
next to the onigiri,

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:14.580
cause at the end I want
everything to be beautiful.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.090
What do I got next on the list?

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:19.510
Oh, I gotta cook a
chicken or was it a duck?

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.140
- [Élise Voiceover] It was a
duck, but I bought a chicken.

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.470
So I took that thang and I seasoned it up

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:24.720
gave it a little rub.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:27.170
And then I put it in
the oven at 350 degrees

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:29.370
for like 40 minutes and
it came out all nice

00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:32.880
and golden and tasted delicious. Okay!

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:35.337
I'm going to do a little
traditional yakiniku, okay.

00:07:35.337 --> 00:07:38.190
Naruto, Shikamaru, Choji,

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.670
you know, they always be at the barbecue.

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:42.060
I'm tryin' to partake in that.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:45.180
I realized I probably can't
light a fire inside the house

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:46.840
like a lit, lit fire for real.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:50.200
So I just ended up using a
grill pan, got my seasoned meat

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.670
put a little onions up on there

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:55.270
and then I grilled in just
like they did at the barbecue.

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:56.780
- [Élise Voiceover] Y'all
I really be whipping it up

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:59.510
in the kitchen and it tasted divine.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.640
- Alright. It is finally time.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:04.970
Everything with the
ramen has been complete.

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:06.040
- [Élise Voiceover] I strained the broth

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.810
after about 11 and a half hours.

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:10.680
And I also made a Tare, which
is used to season the broth

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.820
and give it that nice deep umami flavor.

00:08:12.820 --> 00:08:17.820
- I have all my things to
assemble my ichiraku ramen

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:20.020
the noodles, the eggs, the Naruto,

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:22.430
the bamboo shoot, the green
onions, the pork belly,

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:24.483
the seaweed, the tare, the broth!

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:27.298
Everything is here.

00:08:27.298 --> 00:08:31.180
♪Let's assemble baby girl ♪

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:33.970
Okay. So first you start with the tare,

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:37.380
which has been seasoned so nicely

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:40.110
to give it that nice umami salty flavor.

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:43.110
Ooh. Yeah, let's get a
little bit of the broth.

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:46.350
Oh, this broth that we
spent 12 hours with.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.080
Let's place some noodles in there.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.580
Oh, now we can do the rest of the stuff.

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:53.380
- [Élise Voiceover] Just
placing everything nicely

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.530
to make my beautiful ichiraku ramen.

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:58.410
Oh my God, Naruto would be so proud.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.003
- Oh my God!

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:03.763
The moment we've all been waiting for.

00:09:03.763 --> 00:09:04.950
I just want to take a bite now.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:07.891
It's been a long 12 hours.

00:09:07.891 --> 00:09:10.930
♪It was worth it ♪

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.823
Yes, absolutely.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:18.642
Wow! I cooked every
single dish from Naruto.

00:09:18.642 --> 00:09:19.475
(DJ scratch)

00:09:19.475 --> 00:09:22.100
- [Élise Voiceover]
Unfortunately, I am a liar.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.330
I definitely forgot a few key recipes.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.540
Like some of the dishes
from Itachi's feast.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:28.940
I didn't show you guys how
I made the Curry of Life.

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:31.000
How could I forget the
meal that Sasuke and Naruto

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.580
were eating during the first
major arc of the series?

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:37.960
I, in fact, did not make
every single dish from Naruto,

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:38.830
but I tried.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.040
- Guys, you guys can see there's a lot

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.380
of traditional Japanese food that

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.740
did appear in Naruto other
than his trademark ramen,

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:49.030
Oh, you know one thing I did
forget, Jiraiya's Popsicle.

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:50.450
This was a hard challenge,

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.500
but it was a lot of fun.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.540
My little Naruto!

00:09:54.540 --> 00:09:58.181
Itadakimasu and thank
you guys for watching.

00:09:58.181 --> 00:10:00.764
(upbeat music)

